WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.481
Military Housing Crisis.

00:00:02.431 --> 00:00:11.011
Canadian Armed Forces families live in substandard military housing while the Department of National Defence spends thirty-five point seven billion dollars annually.

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:19.136
Military families report mould, pest infestations, broken heating systems, and maintenance requests that go unanswered for months or years.

00:00:19.136 --> 00:00:23.034
The Military Ombudsman has documented the housing crisis.

00:00:23.034 --> 00:00:25.590
The Auditor General has flagged it.

00:00:25.590 --> 00:00:27.465
Nothing changes.

00:00:27.465 --> 00:00:29.113
The conditions.

00:00:29.113 --> 00:00:49.170
Military families posted to bases across Canada describe Residential Housing Units with persistent mould in bathrooms and basements, pest infestations including mice and cockroaches, broken heating and cooling systems during Canadian winters and summers, maintenance requests submitted and ignored for months, and housing stock built in the nineteen fifties and sixties that has never been adequately renovated.

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:51.852
The military institution pattern.

00:00:51.852 --> 00:00:54.874
Eliminate cognitive testing for recruits.

00:00:54.874 --> 00:00:57.215
Degrade housing for families.

00:00:57.215 --> 00:00:59.749
Offer MAID to veterans seeking help.

00:00:59.749 --> 00:01:03.749
Close military police investigations into senior officers.

00:01:03.749 --> 00:01:08.306
Deploy combat forces to Latvia while domestic infrastructure collapses.

00:01:08.306 --> 00:01:11.238
Each thread is documented independently.

00:01:11.238 --> 00:01:19.999
Together they describe an institution that is systematically degrading its own capability while the government it serves expands surveillance and enforcement powers domestically.
